+# satelle substrate review gives any repo an in-depth review of its substrate
+# against the constitution, its codebase and its story history
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. `satelle substrate review` writes a report listing every substrate item
+   with its origin, a disposition and the evidence for it, any item the judge
+   omits shown as "not judged"; proven by a CLI test over a fixture repo with
+   a stubbed judge.
+2. Each disposition's evidence cites the repo's story history (rejections and
+   reasons, amendments, parks, rework, flaky reruns, dissent), proven by a
+   fixture-ledger test.
+3. The report lists every constitution rule with a file:line finding, "no
+   finding" or "not judged", proven by a stubbed-judge fixture test.
+
+## Design (decided)
+
+- **Judgement:** a new embedded skill `satelle-substrate-review`, dispatched
+  through a seam `newSubstrateJudge` to the repo's plan-review reviewer seat.
+- **What the receiving seat reads for itself:** that seat has a read grant
+  over the repo, the satelle CLI, and every substrate item on disk. So the
+  dispatch carries the instruction and a manifest only: each item's kind,
+  name, origin and path, each constitution rule's name, the per-item counts
+  computed in Go, and the commands to pull the rest (`satelle doc get <kind>
+  <name>`, `satelle ledger list --story <id>`). No item text, rule body or
+  rejection note is copied into the payload; the seat reads the ones it
+  judges.
+- **Proof:** the stubbed-judge tests assert the payload carries the manifest
+  and no item body.
